  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "How to read the three roles",
      "items": [
        "Boundary is what the customer touches. It never reaches an entity directly",
        "Control coordinates. Every rule and every ordering decision lives here",
        "Entities are the stored things. They know their own state and nothing about screens"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "One object owns the seat count",
      "items": [
        "TicketTier is the only lifeline that changes remaining or sold",
        "reserveAtomic is a single indivisible step, so no two requests can both succeed",
        "This is why the same seat cannot be sold twice"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Control asks before it captures",
      "items": [
        "After the provider authorises, control asks the reservation stillHeld()",
        "Only a yes turns the hold into a confirmed order",
        "A no voids the authorisation instead, so the customer is never charged for nothing"
      ]
    }
  ]
